You can easily save them as text files using the download handler function.

In server.R add in a new output function:

  output$textOut <- downloadHandler(
    filename = function() {paste(<NAME>, ".txt", sep="")},
    content = function(file) {
      write(<what you want to save to file>, file)})

And then in the ui.R, you will need to add some kind of button to download.

downloadButton("textOut", label="Download text file")

I don't know about saving as a .doc that preserves HTML formatting, so sorry if this is no help at all.

