Sorry but addResourcePath can only be used to register sub-paths of the Shiny app; it can't be used to serve up a folder directly at the root directory of the app URL. So you could use it for serving up JS for sure, but for the main HTML you'll still need separate files (you could just have a ui.R that calls shinyUI(includeHTML("../base/www/index.html")) though).

