Yes, this is possible. You'll need to use uiOutput/renderUI <http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/dynamic-ui.html> to render the buttons, each with a different ID (e.g. downloadData1 through downloadDataN). For defining the download handlers dynamically, use a pattern like:

observe({
  lapply(1:N, function(i) {
    output[[paste0("downloadData", i)]] <- downloadHandler(...)
  })
})

the important thing there being that you can assign to output[[id]] if your output names are dynamic.

