>> If you set up Shiny Server as autouser/user_apps (see the configuration overview) then RStudio Server and Shiny Server will automatically share the same package library for each user. So each user can install packages using RStudio Server and they will be available to their own Shiny apps. This is how we run glimmer.rstudio.com <http://glimmer.rstudio.com>.
>>
>> You as the superuser can also install libraries in the system-wide R library, which will again be available to both RStudio and Shiny. To do this, run "sudo su - R" and install whatever packages you want from that R prompt, and they should be installed in the system-wide library.
