Hi,

I'm grateful for the recent additions to leaflet-shiny <https://github.com/jcheng5/leaflet-shiny> (geojson) but I've been having difficulty for quite some time with adding overlays to my map. In particular, I need WMS layers.

Barring the inclusions of methods for WMS Tilelayers and control.layers into the main branch of the package, is there a way to inject custom JS code into the JS script generated by leaflet-shiny in the application or a way to alter the source code so that it will show these overlays? The selectable layers themselves are static.

Here's an HTML/JS example:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Leaflet GeoJSON Example</title>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="http://cdn.leafletjs.com/leaflet-0.7.3/leaflet.css" />
</head>
<body>
<div id="map" style="width: 600px; height: 600px"></div>
<script src="http://cdn.leafletjs.com/leaflet-0.7.3/leaflet.js"></script>
<script>
        var nexrad = L.tileLayer.wms("http://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/cgi-bin/wms/nexrad/n0r.cgi", {
        layers: 'nexrad-n0r-900913',
        format: 'image/png',
        transparent: true,
        attribution: "Weather data © 2012 IEM Nexrad"
        });
        var OpenMapSurfer_Roads = L.tileLayer('http://openmapsurfer.uni-hd.de/tiles/roads/x={x}&y={y}&z={z} <http://openmapsurfer.uni-hd.de/tiles/roads/x=%7Bx%7D&y=%7By%7D&z=%7Bz%7D>', {
            minZoom: 0,maxZoom: 20,
            attribution: 'Imagery from <a href="http://giscience.uni-hd.de/">GIScience Research Group @ University of Heidelberg</a> &mdash; Map data &copy; <a href="http://openstreetmap.org">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors, <a href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/">CC-BY-SA</a>'
        });
        var MapQuestOpen_Aerial = L.tileLayer('http://oatile{s}.mqcdn.com/tiles/1.0.0/sat/{z}/{x}/{y}.jpg <http://mqcdn.com/tiles/1.0.0/sat/%7Bz%7D/%7Bx%7D/%7By%7D.jpg>', {
      attribution: 'Tiles Courtesy of <a href="http://www.mapquest.com/">MapQuest</a> &mdash; Portions Courtesy NASA/JPL-Caltech and U.S. Depart. of Agriculture, Farm Service Agency',
      subdomains: '1234'
        });
var map = L.map('map', {
center: [29.53, -95.89],
zoom: 4,
layers: [OpenMapSurfer_Roads]
});
var baseLayers = {
            "MapQuestOpen_Aerial": MapQuestOpen_Aerial,
"OpenMapSurfer_Roads": OpenMapSurfer_Roads
};
        var overlays = {
            "Precipitation": nexrad.addTo(map)
};
L.control.layers(baseLayers, overlays).addTo(map);
</script>
</body>
</html>

You can see that by using an IDE that includes a server such as Brackets, or by running it in R-Studio as an index.html.

Any help in this matter would be greatly greatly appreciated.

